    <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;" color="#000000">
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 2px !important;">
    Gulf strikes intensify
  </h2>
</mj-text>
<mj-image
  border-radius="10px"
  padding="10px 12px"
  width="600px"
  src="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
  alt="Gulf strikes intensify"
  href="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/"
/>
<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>What’s happening?</strong> Strikes in the Middle East have intensified as Iran and joint Israeli-US forces launched <a href="https://edition.cnn.com/world/live-news/iran-war-us-israel-trump-03-03-26" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none;
                border-bottom: 2px solid #4d3060;
                color: black;">new waves of missile</a> and drone attacks. Iranian-backed militias targeted US assets across Gulf countries. The US State Department is advising its citizens in 14 countries, including Saudi Arabia, the UAE, Israel, and Qatar, to <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cpd8ygee9e3o" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none;
                border-bottom: 2px solid #4d3060;
                color: black;">depart immediately</a> as security warnings put embassies on lockdown.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>On the ground:</strong> A consulate in Dubai, a CIA station in Saudi Arabia, and a US base in Qatar all sustained hits. The US has lost nearly $2B worth of military equipment amid its military operations against Iran in the first 4 days of strikes against Iran. Losses include SATCOM terminals, F-15E Strike Eagles, and radar equipment. Six US service members died in <a href="https://www.yahoo.com/news/world/live/iran-live-updates-americans-killed-by-retaliatory-strike-identified-trump-administration-pledges-to-unleash-more-attacks-142632538.html" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none;
                border-bottom: 2px solid #4d3060;
                color: black;">retaliatory strikes</a>. Iran repeatedly targeted Erbil International Airport in Iraq, hosting US forces.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>What’s next?</strong> The US State Department is arranging military and charter flights to evacuate American citizens from the Middle East. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio warned that the most severe US military actions are still to come, with the next phase expected to be even more punishing for Iran. Meanwhile, Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps said recent leadership losses have strengthened its resolve, vowing its enemies will no longer be safe anywhere.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong><em>Fact:</em></strong><em> Between 500,000 and 1Mn US nationals are estimated to be living in the Middle East.</em></p>
</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>

